            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardial infarction after selective portal-systemic shunt.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of myocardial infarction following a distal splenorenal shunt, a selective portal-systemic shunt, in a cirrhotic patient is reported. The post-operative cardiac morbidity was probably related to the hyperdynamic cardiovascular state associated with liver cirrhosis and the increase in intramyocardial tension upon formation of the distal splenorenal shunt.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
